WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.388 --> 00:00:15.457
"Ssss!" hissed as the monkeys ran in terror.

2
00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:18.899
Some of the monkeys had never met Kaa before.

3
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.582
But they'd all heard stories about the terrifying python.

4
00:00:25.163 --> 00:00:28.986
He could slip along branches as quietly as moss grows.

5
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:34.734
As the monkeys fled, Baloo drew in a deep breath of relief.

6
00:00:35.594 --> 00:00:38.135
He was sore and battered after fighting them.

7
00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:40.417
Bagheera was hurt too.

8
00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:46.020
The panther climbed out of the water tank and shook out his wet fur.

9
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.823
"Let's get Mowgli before those monkeys attack again," Bagheera said.

10
00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:55.925
"They will not attack again while I'm here!"

11
00:00:56.406 --> 00:00:57.286
Kaa hissed.

12
00:00:58.247 --> 00:01:00.288
"Where is the man cub anyway?"

13
00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:02.133
"In here!"

14
00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:05.475
Mowgli danced around inside the dome.

15
00:01:05.575 --> 00:01:07.897
"I'm trapped!"

16
00:01:08.337 --> 00:01:12.900
"Please get him out of here," said a snake at his feet.

17
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.602
"He will crush our young."

18
00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:22.166
back, Mowgli," Kaa ordered.

19
00:01:22.847 --> 00:01:25.168
The python looked carefully at the dome.

20
00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:28.831
Finally he spotted a crack in the marble.

21
00:01:29.832 --> 00:01:35.772
Then, lifting his body high above the ground, he smashed down again and again.

22
00:01:35.792 --> 00:01:42.316
"Whoa!" Bagheera exclaimed as the marble shattered in a cloud of dust.

23
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:47.480
Mowgli leaped out and threw himself at Baloo and Bagheera.

24
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.542
"Are you okay?"

25
00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:50.742
Baloo asked.

26
00:01:50.762 --> 00:01:56.366
"I'm sore and hungry," Mowgli replied.

27
00:01:56.386 --> 00:01:58.208
"But I'm fine."

28
00:02:00.244 --> 00:02:01.764
Kaa stared at Mowgli.

29
00:02:03.025 --> 00:02:05.185
"So you're the man cub.

30
00:02:05.806 --> 00:02:08.186
Why, you look like a monkey!"

31
00:02:09.747 --> 00:02:10.687
Mowgli bowed.

32
00:02:10.707 --> 00:02:15.568
"Thank you for saving my life and my friends' lives."

33
00:02:16.528 --> 00:02:19.689
"It's nothing," Kaa said softly.

34
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.810
By now the moon had sunk behind the hills.

35
00:02:24.891 --> 00:02:29.452
Trembling monkeys huddled together on the wall and along the stone buildings.

36
00:02:30.452 --> 00:02:35.576
Kaa glided into the center of the terrace and closed his jaws with a snap.

37
00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:43.041
Terrified, the monkeys watched him begin a slow dance.

38
00:02:43.061 --> 00:02:48.505
"This is my dance called the Hunger of Kaa.

39
00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:51.447
Sit still and watch me!"

40
00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:53.309
the snake commanded.

41
00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:57.492
Kaa wove his head from right to left.

42
00:02:59.552 --> 00:03:01.873
He made slow loops with his body.

43
00:03:03.874 --> 00:03:06.896
His scales rustled.

44
00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:09.137
Mowgli stood with Baloo and Bagheera.

45
00:03:09.778 --> 00:03:12.659
His eyes flicked from the monkeys to his friends.

46
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.722
Everyone was watching the snake with wonder.

47
00:03:18.182 --> 00:03:19.083
Kaa hissed.

48
00:03:19.603 --> 00:03:27.908
"Come closer, monkeys The monkeys swayed forward helplessly.

49
00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:31.486
Baloo and Bagheera began to pitch forward too.

50
00:03:32.287 --> 00:03:33.828
Mowgli sprang toward them.

51
00:03:33.848 --> 00:03:35.670
"Come on!"

52
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.751
he cried, yanking them away.

53
00:03:37.771 --> 00:03:40.854
"Let's get out of here!"

54
00:03:41.775 --> 00:03:46.698
The two great beasts jumped as if Mowgli had just woken them from a dream.

55
00:03:47.579 --> 00:03:50.201
Then they ran a short distance away.

56
00:03:54.365 --> 00:03:57.127
Bagheera glanced back at the snake and shuddered.

57
00:03:59.008 --> 00:04:01.790
"The monkeys aren't the only ones who are scared of Kaa.

58
00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:04.071
That snake makes me nervous."

59
00:04:05.352 --> 00:04:06.953
Baloo shook out his fur.

60
00:04:06.973 --> 00:04:09.514
"It worked out fine.

61
00:04:09.795 --> 00:04:11.215
We have Mowgli again."

62
00:04:11.235 --> 00:04:16.619
"True, but this little adventure cost us," Bagheera said sternly.

63
00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:18.980
"We're both injured.

64
00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.882
Which means we cannot hunt for several days.

65
00:04:22.882 --> 00:04:25.404
And we were forced to ask Kaa for protection."

66
00:04:27.808 --> 00:04:29.188
He glared at Mowgli.

67
00:04:29.208 --> 00:04:31.849
"We warned you about this.

68
00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:35.050
We told you it was foolish to play with the monkeys."

69
00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.151
Mowgli looked down.

70
00:04:37.171 --> 00:04:39.331
"I'm sorry."

71
00:04:39.351 --> 00:04:43.912
"He's very young," Baloo said.

72
00:04:43.932 --> 00:04:47.213
"And he's sorry for what he's done."

73
00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:51.434
"Being sorry is not enough punishment for breaking the rules!"

74
00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:52.995
Bagheera replied.

75
00:04:56.476 --> 00:05:00.205
With that, he gave Mowgli some light taps on the shoulder.

76
00:05:00.225 --> 00:05:02.887
"There," Bagheera said.

77
00:05:02.907 --> 00:05:04.267
"That's done."

78
00:05:07.028 --> 00:05:10.750
According to the law of the jungle, a punishment settled things.

79
00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:16.152
There was no need to say anything more about Mowgli's mistake with the monkeys.

80
00:05:16.172 --> 00:05:20.655
"Jump on my back, Little Brother," Bagheera said.

81
00:05:20.675 --> 00:05:22.035
"We will go home."

82
00:05:23.016 --> 00:05:28.050
"Okay." Mowgli climbed onto Bagheera's back and lay down his head.

83
00:05:31.656 --> 00:05:33.759
Soon he was fast asleep.
